{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/903306-what-would-you-like-to-see-in-dark-eras-2","id":903306,"title":"What would you like to see in Dark Eras 2?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-29T23:59:45-07:00","id":903306,"title":"What would you like to see in Dark Eras 2?","content":"With the release of the book to everyone, I'm definitely curious about whether or not we've seen the last of Dark Eras. Assuming we get another such book with a similar format, are there any settings you're eager to see?<br /> <br /> I've mentioned elsewhere why I think the Meiji period in Japan is such a good fit for Werewolf; the rapid modernization of the country at the cost of tradition and regular culture has some obvious parallels with the myth of Father Wolf needing to die at his children's hands, and the Shadow of the time is no doubt in turmoil is ancient and powerful kami face off against young spirits of technology and foreign influence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T02:17:42-07:00","id":903348,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see them wait till all the CoD gamelines have been updated to 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T02:18:52-07:00","id":903350,"title":"","content":"I'd like a Canadian Dark Era. Perhaps during confederation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T02:42:22-07:00","id":903358,"title":"","content":"This might be too recent, but Somalia 2005-2010 as a Hunter / Changeling / Geist crossover. (Leviathan would work better than Geist, but I imagine fangames aren't getting into Dark Ears)<br /> <br /> The pirates would be loosely aligned with Geist, with a strong use of the metaphor <s>failed state</s> dead state. Bonepickers trying to survive on the scraps of meat still left on Somalia's bones. Though their would be a significant minority of foreign Sin-Eaters who see a beauty and opportunity in the dead state that those who haven't experienced death cannot see.<br /> <br /> Hunters would be the international coalition, <u>heavily</u> skewed towards VALKYRIE and their goal is simple; stop piracy and protect international trade. Though with a sideline in rescuing hostages and such to acquire sympathy points.<br /> <br /> Broadly speaking both sides will be portrayed as reasonable people, who due to circumstances find themselves in conflict. The real source of the problem would be politicians who're portrayed as distant and isolated from the effects their policies have.<br /> <br /> <br /> Meanwhile the Changelings are a third party who appear to come out of nowhere, raid, vanish, and make absolutely no sense to either the Hunters or Sin-Eaters. They act like they're straight out of Pirates of the Caribbean with a strong faerie logic twist. They might raid a cruse ship, attacking it with a wooden galleon and cannon, only to vanish after stealing one single piece of jewellery. Or allow themselves to be captured by the navy, flirt outrageously with the hunters, then vanish the moment they score. In personalty they range from lovable Jack Sparrow types to murderous Black-beard types yet seem to have very little infighting. All that's known for sure is that they really dislike hostage takers (which includes hunters arresting pirates) but they can express that hostility through means as overt as making you walk the plank to as underhanded witty insults that stick in your head and drive you mad.<br /> <br /> In fact, neither the Hunters or the Sin-Eaters even know that the Changelings are Changelings. If they did it would make sense. They're engaged in Talecrafting on an enormous scale. They commit acts of piracy on Earth to demonstrate their piracy and swashbuckling chops to the Wyrd, then cash in that reputation to pull of tropes like &quot;<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JgWJUKzgvR4\" target=\"_blank\">A witty swashbuckling pirate can thumb his nose at powerful authority</a>&quot;, &quot;pirates raid trading lines&quot;, and &quot;pirate crews were full of freed slaves&quot; in order to run an enormous and successful piracy campaign on multiple Hedge trading routes, freeing slaves and freshly taken captives by the shipfull.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-30-2016, 05:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T06:26:09-07:00","id":903434,"title":"","content":"Innocents: The Blitz<br /> <br /> Also, someone on last week's Monday Meeting Notes brought up Star Wars Dark Eras, and while that's not even a little bit possible, I've never wanted anything more in my entire life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T06:58:40-07:00","id":903449,"title":"","content":"*cough*StarTrekDarkEraswouldbecooler.*cough*<br /> <br /> Innocents The Blitz too here, although Christ, hasn't this thread been made, like, fifty times before now?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.